  "slug": "machine-learning-assisted-83b8",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and a proteomics tool release package reproducible data preparation steps ahead of downstream analysis.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is open-source software that prepares and structures data before statistical or biological inference. NBDC Data Tools builds reproducible, analysis-ready datasets from ABCD and HBCD study releases in R and Python using standardized processing. gcat, a C++ library for genomic coordinate work, and its_a_scam, a modular single-cell toolkit covering count matrix generation and per-cell quality control, address upstream data handling in genomics and transcriptomics. WorkListGenerator, a CLI tool, structures proteomics project metadata and block-randomizes LC-MS run order for experiment scheduling. What is new is the scope: scripted, reproducible preparation steps are now released across cohort, sequencing, and mass spectrometry workflows rather than as isolated utilities.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-10"
}
